# Lecture 13B

## Chromosome Abnormalities: Inversions

## Chapter 9

## Dr. Neil Voss

## December 8, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Distinguish paracentric and pericentric inversions.
- Trace homolog pairing within an inversion loop.
- Predict chromosome products after crossing over.
- Relate chromosome position to gene expression.

=== layout: section

# Chromosome Abnormalities: Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

# *Alterations of Chromosome Structure*

@body

- Breakage of a chromosome can lead to four types of changes in chromosome structure
  - [*Deletion*]{underline=true} removes a chromosomal segment
  - [*Duplication*]{underline=true} repeats a segment
  - [*Inversion*]{color=red underline=true} [reverses orientation of a segment within a chromosome]{color=red}
  - [*Translocation*]{underline=true} moves a segment from one chromosome to another

=== layout: section

# Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

# *Inversion*

@body

![Slide image 1](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/inversion_overview.drawn.svg)

- An inversion reverses a segment within a chromosome.

=== layout: two-panels

# *Ectopic Recombination resulting in inversion*

@left

![Slide image 2](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/image_002.png)

@right

- Blue and pink are inverted repeats
- They couple in reverse orientation
- Resulting in an inverted gene sequence
  - A B &#8230; Y Z
  - &#8594; Z Y &#8230; B A

=== layout: two-panels

# *Homologous chromosome pairing with an inversion*

@left

![Slide image 3](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/inversion-synapsis.drawn.svg)

@right

- In an organism that carries a wildtype chromosome some and a inverted chromosome
- the gene-for-gene attraction during synapsis causes
- one of the chromosomes to form into a loop in the region in which the gene order is inverted.

=== layout: two-over-one-panels

# *No crossing over in an inversion loop = good*

@top-left

![Slide image 4](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/image_004.png)

@top-right

![Slide image 5](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/image_005.png)

@bottom

- If there is no crossing over within the inversion loop, then the homologous chromosomes disjoin without problems.

