- comparing (a) to (b) inversion of f-e-d-c to c-d-e-f
- from this the evolutionary history is c &#8594; d &#8594; a &#8594; b

=== layout: section

# Position-effect Variegation (PEV)

=== layout: one-panel

# *Position-effect Variegation (PEV)*

@body

- Expression of a gene can be affected by its position on the chromosome.
  - most often whether a gene is in or near heterochromatin.

![Slide image 21](assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/position-effect-chromosomes.drawn.svg)

